## Formula Task Protocol Used by Tasks 4-8 and 10-14

Every experimental formula task follows this exact sequence:

1. re-read the complete current authority preflight;
2. add one failing, formula-specific contract test;
3. define identity, pleasure mechanism, exclusions, architecture, planes, textures, transitions, pressure/release, and recurrence before any dose;
4. complete source row/module dispositions and all donor manifests;
5. write at least 58 ideal rows totaling 6,000 target parts or uL-equivalent parts;
6. run the missing-chemical impact gate before writing the current build;
7. write one flat current table totaling exactly 6,000 uL, with no direct raw-stock row below 10 uL and no quantitatively held material;
8. audit active ppm, ODT, composite-natural OAV, five temporal windows, takeover, adaptation, redundancy, suppression, under-threshold role claims, and stock rebase;
9. run the focused test and deterministic donor audit;
10. run the release gate once with a unique audit path, capture `pipeline.json`, render `pipeline_analysis.md`, and append the same full analysis under `## Pipeline Analysis` in the formula artifact;
11. retain all FAIL/WARN/HOLD findings and revise only through target-linked constant-total changes;
12. commit the formula, its focused-test addition, and its three-file verification bundle together.

For each task, assign `$formulaPath`, `$pipelinePath`, `$analysisPath`, and `$auditPath` from the exact row in the diagnostic-run matrix below, then run:

```powershell
$env:PERFUME_PIPELINE_AUDIT_PATH = $auditPath
python scripts\formula_release_gate.py --formula-file $formulaPath --expected-concentrate-ul 6000 --batch-volume-ml 30 --brief auto --json --append-analysis | Set-Content -LiteralPath $pipelinePath -Encoding utf8
python scripts\format_pipeline_analysis.py --input $pipelinePath | Set-Content -LiteralPath $analysisPath -Encoding utf8
```

